To solve the problem of determining the individual weights of the five bales from their pair sums, we can model the problem using constraints in MiniZinc. The approach involves ensuring all possible pairs of the five bales sum to the given values and that the bales are ordered.

```minizinc
% Define the given pair sums
array[1..10] of int: given_sums = [80, 82, 83, 84, 85, 86, 87, 88, 90, 91];

% Variables for the bales' weights, sorted in non-decreasing order
array[1..5] of var int: bales;
constraint increasing(bales);

% Generate all possible pair sums and ensure they match the given sorted sums
array[1..10] of var int: pair_sums;
constraint
    forall(i in 1..5, j in i+1..5) (
        pair_sums[(i-1)*(10 - i) div 2 + (j - i)] = bales[i] + bales[j]
    ) /\
    sorted(pair_sums) = given_sums;

% Solve and output the solution
solve satisfy;

output [
    "{",
    "\"bales\": [" ++ join(", ", [show(bales[i]) | i in 1..5]) ++ "]",
    "}"
];
```

